{
  "summary": {
    "notes": "### Font families\n- **Roboto** (variable, weights 100–900) — the only face used on the homepage. Self-hosted through `next/font`: `/_next/static/media/roboto_latin_wght-s.p.4075f395.woff2` (67,264 bytes, WOFF2, `font-display: swap`, preloaded). CSS family name `roboto`, applied on `<body>` via class `roboto_51c32070-module__YpxGXa__className`.\n- Fallback metric-matched face **\"roboto Fallback\"** = `local(Arial)` with `ascent-override: 92.43%; descent-override: 24.32%; line-gap-override: 0%; size-adjust: 100.37%` (prevents layout shift).\n- Also declared but **not used on the homepage**: `robotoTool`, `robotoBlog` (same Roboto file, aliases for other pages) and **Solitreo** 400 (`solitreo_latin_400-s.p.8dc56742.woff2`, 25,944 bytes) — preloaded on the homepage but never rendered (`document.fonts` status \"unloaded\").\n- Weights in use: 400, 500, 600, 700. No italics. Text is `-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased` (Tailwind `antialiased` on the root wrapper).\n\n### Behaviour\n- Fluid sizes with `clamp()` above 768px (story headline `clamp(2.75rem, 4.45vw, 4rem)`, body `clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.8rem)`, sub-headline `clamp(2rem, 3.05vw, 2.75rem)`); fixed sizes below 768px.\n- Orphan control: JS \"glue\" spans (`data-glue`) keep the last two words of each line together (`white-space: nowrap`) and are re-balanced by a ResizeObserver.\n- Uppercase is applied only with CSS `text-transform` (source copy is sentence case).",
